From: tinker-edge-r-debian
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: fan53555: accept Fairchild option 00 revision 0xc

The Tinker Edge R (RK3399Pro) has FAN53555 regulators (vdd_cpu_b, vdd_gpu,
I2C address 0x60) that report chip ID 0, revision 0xc. The driver refuses
them ("Chip ID 0 with rev 12 not supported"), so vdd_gpu and vdd_cpu_b never
probe and panfrost and cpufreq stay deferred.

The vendor 4.4 kernel handles this revision as 600 mV + N * 12.5 mV; use the
same range here.

Signed-off-by: tinker-edge-r-debian
---
--- a/drivers/regulator/fan53555.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/fan53555.c
@@ -113,6 +113,7 @@
 enum {
 	FAN53555_CHIP_REV_00 = 0x3,
 	FAN53555_CHIP_REV_13 = 0xf,
+	FAN53555_CHIP_REV_23 = 0xc,
 };
 
 enum {
@@ -305,6 +306,11 @@
 			di->vsel_step = 10000;
 			di->enable_time = 400;
 			break;
+		case FAN53555_CHIP_REV_23:
+			di->vsel_min = 600000;
+			di->vsel_step = 12500;
+			di->enable_time = 400;
+			break;
 		default:
 			dev_err(di->dev,
 				"Chip ID %d with rev %d not supported!\n",
